<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arabia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arabian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arabia is the region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula">Arabian Peninsula</a> in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, bounded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>. It was the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and the starting point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>'s conquests. Its ports and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> routes linked it to the Aksumite, Babylonian and Chaldean worlds, and its coasts were part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade">Indian Ocean trade</a> networks used by states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arabia.jpg" alt="Arabia" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SeaWiFS Project, NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center, and ORBIMAGE · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arabian_Peninsula_dust_SeaWiFS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
